# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads as the build context.
#
# Without this file gcloud uploads everything — and normally it would fall back
# to .gitignore, but this directory is not a git repository, so there is no
# fallback. That means 340MB, 220MB of it a .venv the image rebuilds anyway.
#
# The Dockerfile copies pyproject.toml, README.md, uv.lock and src/. Everything
# below is either irrelevant to the image or actively unwanted in it.

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
build/

# Never upload local secrets. .env is gitignored but gitignore is not consulted
# here, so it has to be named explicitly.
.env
*.pem
*-key.json
credentials*.json

# Not needed to build or run the service. scripts/ is kept whole (140KB) rather
# than excluded-with-an-exception for build_form_fields.py: a negated pattern
# fails silently — rename the file and the PDF simply is not in the context, and
# the build breaks somewhere further along with no mention of the ignore file.
tests/
docs/
n8n/
terraform/
.claude/
.idea/
.DS_Store
